[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: ROO User Requirements (USR)
UID: DOC-ROO-USR
VERSION: 0.1

[SECTION]
TITLE: About

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Project: ROO (gym = ROOGuildApp / live product VALHALLA).
SoT: Develop@a8a1edd713d6db6db61d42ed4eacf6a9e8737d07.
Source: SSOT requirements/usr (published only).
Phase 1 complete: USR-ROO-001 .. USR-ROO-042 (42 nodes).
STATUS Active means published in SSOT registry, not proven by evidence.
<<<

[SECTION]
TITLE: Platform/Auth (USR-ROO-001 .. USR-ROO-005)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: USR-ROO-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Platform health and safe boot
STATEMENT: >>>
Operators and deploy pipelines need the API process to refuse to start without required secrets, migrate schema, start the Discord bot, and expose a health check that reflects DB reachability.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Avoid silent half-starts and false-online production.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
domain: Platform/Auth
who: Platform operators / deploy
why: Avoid silent half-starts and false-online production.
spoken_constraints: Develop live behavior only
ssot_status: published
sot: Develop@a8a1edd713d6db6db61d42ed4eacf6a9e8737d07
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: USR-ROO-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Discord OAuth sign-in and callback routing
STATEMENT: >>>
Users must sign in (or sign up) via Discord OAuth and land in the correct post-auth path based on onboarded guild count and intent, including production token-exchange via the Vercel bridge and rate-limit friendly redirects.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Single identity provider; guild membership drives tenant access.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
domain: Platform/Auth
who: End users (members/officers)
why: Single identity provider; guild membership drives tenant access.
spoken_constraints: Scopes identify guilds guilds.members.read; state intent signin|signup
ssot_status: published
sot: Develop@a8a1edd713d6db6db61d42ed4eacf6a9e8737d07
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: USR-ROO-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Session identity and logout
STATEMENT: >>>
Authenticated callers need a stable identity from session or signed profile header, a me endpoint that re-signs profile, and a logout that clears the session cookie.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Cross-origin and cookie fallbacks require dual identity resolution.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
domain: Platform/Auth
who: Authenticated SPA / API clients
why: Cross-origin and cookie fallbacks require dual identity resolution.
spoken_constraints: HMAC verify with DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET for x-user-profile
ssot_status: published
sot: Develop@a8a1edd713d6db6db61d42ed4eacf6a9e8737d07
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: USR-ROO-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: SPA session restore and credentialed API client
STATEMENT: >>>
The browser app must restore session from auth_user query then localStorage (migrating legacy keys), verify via /auth/me, always send credentials, and attach profile/tenant headers; local dev uses Vite proxy.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Survive OAuth redirects and local vs deployed backends.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
domain: Platform/Auth
who: SPA users
why: Survive OAuth redirects and local vs deployed backends.
spoken_constraints: Legacy dynasty_raid_session migrates to guild_raid_session
ssot_status: published
sot: Develop@a8a1edd713d6db6db61d42ed4eacf6a9e8737d07
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: USR-ROO-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Cookie, CORS, and unauthenticated routing
STATEMENT: >>>
Session cookies and CORS must match local HTTP vs deployed HTTPS realities; unauthenticated users hitting protected shells go to landing; /login permanently redirects to /landing; document title reflects product vs guild.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Cross-site cookie and CORS must work with Vercel ↔ Render.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
domain: Platform/Auth
who: SPA + browser security model
why: Cross-site cookie and CORS must work with Vercel ↔ Render.
spoken_constraints: secure/sameSite differ by environment
ssot_status: published
sot: Develop@a8a1edd713d6db6db61d42ed4eacf6a9e8737d07
<<<

